# Earthbend's delayed "When that land dies or is put into exile, return it to the battlefield tapped under your control"
# (CR 701.66a) triggers when the land is exiled, but what it returns is the card in exile (CR 400.7e): a land that has
# already come back is a new object, which the ability doesn't affect (CR 603.7c, 400.7). Bot1's Badgermole Cub
# earthbends its Forest (a 1/1 land creature); Bot1 flickers the Forest with Ephemerate. The return triggers on the exile
# and does nothing: the Forest that Ephemerate returned stays untapped, a land only, and nothing more comes back.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Black Lotus
Badgermole Cub
Mox Pearl
Ephemerate
Forest x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

